{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Frozen-mirror rehearsal reached the live Jira identity gate and failed closed before rewrite. Frozen source tip: fba1098902f1e8943b259fe16dd08167dc69bb7b. Verified backup: /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-comment-echo-artifacts.XpqSZt/tickets-before.bundle with backup-manifest.json; fresh GET-only inventory again reports REB-1567=19, REB-1931=29, REB-2605=8. Manifest builder refused because every one of the six incident body hashes has TWO live Jira copies, not one. Preexisting IDs are 963510/963511/963512, 963788/963789, 964272. Second IDs are 997143/997144/997145, 997255/997256, 997293. Commit ef716a48cee23bafe155ed7cb256ccb49bf316e0 proves the six second identities were imported by reconciler run 32447697242; the RCA on absurd-zoometric-bobwhite records that prior run 32447039101 posted the previously unmapped backlog. All 840 current bindings.comment_ids values are the unknown-ID sentinel, so no authoritative mapping chooses a survivor. Causal provenance—not age—identifies the six 997xxx comments as rollout-created duplicates. Per the approved runbook, I did not mutate Jira, weaken the one-live-copy gate, choose by age, build a manifest, rewrite history, or publish any ref. Preparation is blocked pending explicit authority for a separately backed-up, exact-six Jira cleanup followed by two unchanged production-equivalent reconciler observations. The earlier single-branch frozen-source attempt was also preserved at /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-comment-echo-artifacts.xHomjG; backup correctly refused it because the full heads/tags census was not locally present."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787578044919140001,"uuid":"0f2d1d74-5380-4a5a-96c8-